@startuml on_behalf_of_refusal_sequence
title K9-AIF 1.36.0: a refused tool call travels as an exception, and the orchestrator decides

actor "Caller\n(signed in as hacker)" as Caller
participant "Router" as R
participant "Orchestrator" as O
participant "Squad" as S
participant "Agent" as A
participant "MCP connector" as C
participant "Keycloak" as KC
participant "MCP server" as M

Caller -> R : POST /chat + token
R -> R : admit(): verify, keep token,\nsign identity (hacker)
R -> O : route(payload)
O -> S : execute_squads()\n(caller = hacker)
S -> A : execute()
A -> C : call_tool("get_nuclear_access_code")
C -> KC : token exchange (RFC 8693)
KC --> C : token: hacker, aud = MCP server
C -> M : tools/call + token
M -> M : verify token,\nrole nuclear_officer? no
M --> C : error: refused
C -> A : raises MCPToolError
A -> S : raises ToolRefused (PermissionError)\n(the application's own class)
note right of S : logs the failed step;\nlater steps do not run
S -> O : re-raises
O -> O : catches it:\nstatus "denied", by "nuclear-mcp server"
O --> R : result
R --> Caller : {"status": "denied", "user": "hacker", ...}

note over A, S
  Nothing is returned as if the tool had worked.
  Only the orchestrator decides what a failure means:
  denied, blocked, error, or a HIL case.
end note
@enduml
